Our solution, based on our Atelier platform, a Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) platform, provides an intelligent assistance tool that meets the client's requirements. The Atelier platform consists of several components, including a document-ingestion pipeline, vector store, retrieval layer with hybrid search, orchestration layer, and answer layer. This platform can provide quick access to reliable information by retrieving relevant passages from the client's controlled corpus and generating answers grounded in those passages.

The solution supports drafting professional documents, such as client letters and mission notes, using template-guided drafting capabilities. It also assists with handling client files by providing structured extraction with source linking, allowing users to extract figures and other relevant information from documents and link them to their source passages. Furthermore, the solution facilitates collaboration and mission continuity by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress client file, and efficient resumption by another collaborator.

Our proposed architecture leverages the strengths of our Atelier platform, integrating it with the client's existing tools and infrastructure while ensuring performance, security, and data sovereignty. The solution must sustain its performance during seasonal peak loads and ensure high availability, with a median latency of 1.3 seconds and a p95 latency below 2.5 seconds.

To address confidentiality and security concerns, our organization has implemented several measures to ensure the security and compliance posture of the solution. As an ISO 27001 certified company since 2023, our development, delivery, and operations already adhere to strict information security standards. Additionally, our ISO 27701 certification for privacy information management extension ensures we handle personal data with utmost care.

The solution is hosted within the EU, with no transfer outside, meeting the client's sovereignty requirements. Our hosting partner, OuraneCloud, holds the SecNumCloud qualification at the hosting layer, ensuring that data is protected and compliant with regulatory requirements. We also implement strict partitioning of client files, ensuring no leakage of data between them, and maintain a high level of access control to prevent unauthorized circulation of data.

Our budget for this project is €220,000 over 3 years, which is well within our normal deal range and financial capacity. To optimize costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service, we propose a cost-efficient configuration that protects our gross margin, targeted between 25% and 35%. Our daily rates range from €700 to €1,300 per day, depending on the role, and we can allocate tasks efficiently among team members with different daily rates.

The proposed solution also aligns with Cabinet Vauclair & Associés' environmental expectations and broader CSR goals. As a signatory to the Responsible Tech Charter, we have objectives for gender balance and inclusion and participate in apprenticeship and work-study programs. Our AI ethics principles include human oversight, transparency, bias monitoring, data minimization, and a documented data-use policy.

In conclusion, our consortium's proposal addresses all the requirements and constraints outlined in the call for tenders. We are confident that our solution, based on our Atelier platform, can improve productivity and the quality and reliability of Cabinet Vauclair & Associés' professionals' work while preserving professional secrecy and the reliability of figures. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail and demonstrate how our solution can meet the client's needs.
